  "description" : "[h1]xNeeds[/h1]\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThis mod uses AI! I'd like to warn you beforehand!\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[b]Four survival needs for Starbound — without replacing your HUD.[/b]\n\n[b]xStarbound required[/b] OpenStarbound version at: https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3801345641\n[b]Singleplayer tested only[/b]\n\nThirst, Fatigue, Bladder, and Hygiene are tracked persistently and shown as four thin, scale-aware meters beneath the vanilla or FU hunger bar. Warnings and nonlethal penalties give them weight, while drinks, food, sleep, weather, and biomes keep them moving.\n\n[h2]Features[/h2]\n\n[list]\n[*]Four thin meters with native Starbound icons and hover details\n\n[*]Five configurable tiers (Normal to Critical), with warnings and nonlethal penalties to speed, jump, power, energy regeneration, and protection\n\n[*]Automatic drink and food profiles: water, juice, soda, caffeine, alcohol, salty, toxic, and container returns. Bottled Water, for example, gives back an Empty Bottle.\n\n[*]Day/night Fatigue, a Rested bonus after sleeping, and environment-driven Thirst and Fatigue\n\n[*]Toilets, baths, showers, clean water, rain, combat, and activity all affect your needs\n\n[*]In-game settings menu and built-in help\n[/list]\n\n[h2]In-game commands[/h2]\n\n[list]\n[*][b]/xneeds options[/b] — settings menu for HUD options, gameplay toggles, and difficulty\n\n[*][b]/xneeds help[/b] — topics include needs, tiers, drinks, foods, hygiene, sleep, settings, and commands\n\n[*][b]/xneeds beverage[/b] / [b]/xneeds beverages[/b] — inspect and audit drinks\n\n[*][b]/xneeds food[/b] / [b]/xneeds foods[/b] — inspect and audit food\n[/list]\n\n[h2]Requirements[/h2]\n\n[list]\n[*][b]xStarbound[/b] required. Stock Starbound and OpenStarbound are not supported.\n\n[*]Works with or without [b]Frackin' Universe[/b]\n[/list]\n\n[h2]Compatibility[/h2]\n\nNo vanilla, FU, or FrackinInterface files are replaced. Other mods can register their own drinks and foods through item parameters, and unknown biomes safely fall back to no modifier.\n\n[h2]Notes[/h2]\n\nSingleplayer focused. Needs are stored in the character save. Safe uninstall steps are included in the README.\n\n[h2]About this mod[/h2]\n\nHey guys! This is my first mod upload.\n\nAnd, with the AI out of the way: yes, this mod is completely vibecoded.\n\nI made — ahem — prompted it in one day, over roughly eight hours split between Codex and DeepSeek. I don't really want to hide that, so here's the disclaimer upfront.\n\nIf you find a bug, feel free to tell me. I'll do my best to reproduce it, figure out what went wrong, and then take the whip to the considerably-more-intelligent-than-me AI until it fixes it.\n\nI originally made xNeeds because I felt like doing a little survival roleplay in Starbound.\n\nThen I looked at the clock.\n\nOH DAMN, IT'S ALREADY BEEN A FULL DAY.\n\nWelp.\n\nIt was fun, and apparently the whole thing cost me about $1.12 USD worth of prompting.\n\nI couldn't find a modern Needs mod that did quite what I wanted. The ones I found either had a lot of extra systems I wasn't interested in, were very old, or had vanished along with places like Zippyshare and old Chucklefish Forum downloads.\n\nSo... here is the fruit of my work.\n\nOr, more accurately, the fruit of some Chinese server somewhere, DeepSeek, GPT-5.6 Sol, and one guy repeatedly saying \"okay but what if we add this too?\"",
